* LM393 voltage comparator macro-model (one comparator per .SUBCKT LM393).
*
* Source: copy in github.com/semianalog/mod12003 (sim/LM393.sub). The text is the classic
* "PARTS version 4.03" macro-model of 1990 for the National Semiconductor / TI LM393.
* License: the file carries no license text, so the terms are NOT confirmed. See models/README.md;
* replace it with the current TI model (https://www.ti.com/product/LM393) if redistribution matters.
*
* Changes made in this repository: none to the model; the wrapper LM393_DUAL at the end puts two
* comparators into one package, in the pin order of the KiCad symbol Comparator:LM393.
*
* LM393 VOLTAGE COMPARATOR "MACROMODEL" SUBCIRCUIT
* CREATED USING PARTS VERSION 4.03 ON 03/07/90 AT 14:17
* REV (N/A)
* CONNECTIONS:   NON-INVERTING INPUT
*                | INVERTING INPUT
*                | | POSITIVE POWER SUPPLY
*                | | | NEGATIVE POWER SUPPLY
*                | | | | OPEN COLLECTOR OUTPUT
*                | | | | |
.SUBCKT LM393    1 2 3 4 5
*
  F1    9  3 V1 1
  IEE   3  7 DC 100.0E-6
  VI1  21  1 DC .75
  VI2  22  2 DC .75
  Q1    9 21  7 QIN
  Q2    8 22  7 QIN
  Q3    9  8  4 QMO
  Q4    8  8  4 QMI
.MODEL QIN PNP(IS=800.0E-18 BF=2.000E3)
.MODEL QMI NPN(IS=800.0E-18 BF=1002)
.MODEL QMO NPN(IS=800.0E-18 BF=1000 CJC=1E-15 TR=807.4E-9)
  E1   10  4  9  4  1
  V1   10 11 DC 0
  Q5    5 11  4 QOC
.MODEL QOC NPN(IS=800.0E-18 BF=20.29E3 CJC=1E-15 TF=942.6E-12 TR=543.8E-9)
  DP    4  3 DX
  RP 3  4 46.3E3
.MODEL DX  D(IS=800.0E-18)
*
.ENDS
*
* [eda_agent] Two comparators in one package. Port names follow the package pins of the
* KiCad symbol: 1 OUT1, 2 IN1-, 3 IN1+, 4 GND, 5 IN2+, 6 IN2-, 7 OUT2, 8 VCC.
* The outputs are open collector: they need a pull-up resistor in the circuit.
.SUBCKT LM393_DUAL OUT1 IN1N IN1P GND IN2P IN2N OUT2 VCC
XA IN1P IN1N VCC GND OUT1 LM393
XB IN2P IN2N VCC GND OUT2 LM393
.ENDS
